<title>INDIA: Hindustan Oil 1996/97 net down.</title>
<headline>Hindustan Oil 1996/97 net down.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		5.537  vs  13.393</p>
<p>    Income		   53.075  vs  64.933</p>
<p>    Provision for	  10.00   vs   0.00</p>
<p>contigencies</p>
<p>    Total expenditure    26.269  vs  30.516</p>
<p>Exploration expenses 35.925  vs  30.981</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    4.469  vs   7.524</p>
<p>    Tax			 6.8    vs  13.50</p>
<p>    Gross profit	   26.806  vs  34.417</p>
<p>    Reserves		208.596  vs 203.056</p>
<p>Note: Hindustan Oil Exploration Company Ltd is India's only independent listed oil exploration and production firm.</p>
<p>The company said it had made considerable progress in the PY-3 block, which it is developing with Vaalco India as the operator, with production expected to commence in the third quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
